    <string name="wipe_copy_reach">The copy cannot be loaded back in automatically — reading old records into the new format is a conversion that has to be written by hand. Keep any weights you care about written down somewhere else until backup arrives.</string>
    <string name="wipe_continue">Clear the records and continue</string>

    <!-- ADR-0023's release half of the same screen. Nothing is going to be deleted here: the app
         refuses to open records it cannot read, so this variant is a dead end that names the copy
         and offers to share it. No forward button, because there is nowhere forward to go. -->
    <string name="schema_refused_title">This version cannot open the records on this phone</string>
    <string name="schema_refused_body">The records on this phone were saved by a different version of Binky, and this one cannot read them. Nothing has been deleted.</string>
    <string name="schema_refused_copy_taken">A copy of them is saved on this phone, and stays there:</string>
    <string name="schema_refused_reach">Installing the version that saved them should let you back in. Until then, share the copy somewhere safe — it is the only one.</string>

